From 418136fe7fe52f1469d0955d0ba79d79ac06ea00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Agustin N. Coppari Hollmann" <copparihollmann@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 23:57:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] profile DB: bit-exact FireSim recalibration data + rvv
 mlp_control/yolov8_fused

Preserves measurement data that existed only in the working tree on `garden`, so
it survives a fresh clone elsewhere. Committed on its own branch; the two commits
it sits on (03ee2e2 yolov8_nano hetero cycles, de22a1d dronet hetero cycles) were
also on no remote branch and go up with it.

Contents:

  * 5 recalibrated results.csv under sweep_v8/{V256D128_rvv,gemmini_q31}/
    firesim_rocket_saturn. Values only -- identical dispatch ids, ops and shapes,
    242 insertions against 242 deletions -- i.e. per-dispatch cycle counts
    updated from newer FireSim measurement, not a structural change.
  * new V256D128_rvv/firesim_rocket_saturn profiles for mlp_control and
    yolov8_nano_fused.
  * the *.prebitexact_backup snapshots, which are a DISTINCT third state: they
    differ from the committed HEAD version, so they are not recoverable from
    history and would otherwise be lost.

Deliberately NOT committed: the 5 *.prev20b_backup files. Each is byte-identical
to its committed HEAD version, so git history already holds that state and
tracking them would only add duplicate copies of profile data.

Not used by the freshness study in XPU-RT, which reads
gen/profile/**/firesim_gemmini_opu from the superproject (tracked separately).
This is the recalibration line that commit ae28587's PDB content-hash guard
exists to protect -- the "predicted 70 ms / measured 638 ms" trap.
